{"step_index":290,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:15:22Z","thinking":"**Constructing Core Pages**\n\nI'm now focused on building the foundational pages in the frontend. I've started with `Home.jsx`, crafting the landing page with a live battle preview, hero call-to-action, and feature cards. Next up are `Login.jsx` and `Register.jsx`, aiming for clean, dark authentication forms with immediate validation and error toasts. Then, I will address `Dashboard.jsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Matchmaking Logic**\n\nI'm now diving into the matchmaking process and the components related to a match. The `/versus` page, or `MatchmakingLobby.jsx`, is taking shape. I'm focusing on an interactive matchmaking radar UI, an elapsed seconds ticker, a dynamic rating search, and mode/difficulty/topic selectors. I'll need a websocket implementation for an automatic redirect to `/versus/:matchId` after a match is found. For the `/versus/:matchId` path, I'm sketching out the `VersusArena.jsx` component, a real-time battle arena with a three-column layout, and planning how to incorporate countdowns, opponent data, and server timers.\n\n\n**Expanding User Features**\n\nI'm now expanding the site's feature set. I'm building out `/practice`, `PracticeList.jsx`, a problem bank browser complete with search, filters, and paginated cards. Next up is `/practice/:problemId`, rendering `PracticeWorkspace.jsx`, the standalone Monaco editor-powered problem-solving environment. Then, I'll build out `Leaderboard.jsx` for the `/leaderboard` path with a top 100 global leaderboard, and `MatchHistory.jsx` for `/matches` that has a history list with \"View Analysis\" modals. I'm also planning `ProfileAnalytics.jsx` for user analytics.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import React from 'react';\nimport { Link } from 'react-router-dom';\nimport { Swords, Code2, Zap, Shield, Trophy, Cpu, ArrowRight } from 'lucide-react';\nimport { us